6. Collision Audit

The collision audit verifies that the specific construction \Theta_A(\lambda) = \mu[p_A(T) - p_H^{(q)}(T) \geq \lambda] does not duplicate an existing mathematical object.

Performance profiles (Dolan & Moré, 2002). Survival function \rho_s(\tau) with reference = best solver, threshold = relative time ratio. Distinct from human-relative margin over cognitive task space.

Empirical attainment functions (Fonseca et al., 2011). Coverage \alpha_T(z) over objective space with reference = algorithm ensemble. Distinct from cognitive task space with human reference.

Task-level stochastic dominance. Comparison of AI vs. human CDFs on a single task. No task measure \mu, no margin field M_{A,H}(T), no dominance survival function over structured task space.

Verdict. The pattern of survival/coverage functions over task collections is established. The specific construction of a human-relative margin distribution over a measurable task space has no direct precedent.

\boxed{
\textbf{Novel claim: human-relative stochastic dominance of capability margins over a measurable task space.}
}

