7. Robustness via Optimal Transport

7.1. Ambiguity Sets

Definition 7.1 (Ambiguity Set). With c from Definition 3.3 and W_c the c-Wasserstein distance:

\mathfrak{U}_\varepsilon(\mu) = \left\{\nu \in \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{T}) : W_c(\nu, \mu) \leq \varepsilon\right\}.

7.2. Robust Dominance Survival Function

Definition 7.2.

\boxed{
\Theta_A^{\mathrm{rob}}(\lambda, \varepsilon) = \inf_{\nu \in \mathfrak{U}_\varepsilon(\mu)} \nu\left(\left\{T : M_{A,H}^{(q)}(T) \geq \lambda\right\}\right).
}

Theorem 7.1 (Monotonicity). \varepsilon_1 \leq \varepsilon_2 \implies \Theta_A^{\mathrm{rob}}(\lambda, \varepsilon_1) \geq \Theta_A^{\mathrm{rob}}(\lambda, \varepsilon_2).

Proof. \mathfrak{U}_{\varepsilon_1}(\mu) \subseteq \mathfrak{U}_{\varepsilon_2}(\mu), so the infimum over a larger set is no larger. \square

Proposition 7.2. \Theta_A^{\mathrm{rob}}(\lambda, 0) = \Theta_A(\lambda).

